From bd07e875448830b416f7f7e0a94436ed61dfeb01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:50:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Evolver: Expressive Studio's Bento Bloom home

Draw Expressive Studio's home in ExpressiveOS's Bloom colours, as the
bento layout picked for it: the lock screen as it is now (its wallpaper
and clock face) beside the themes and wallpaper tiles, then the colours
and fonts tiles, the clock styles and what's new cards, and a grid of
the other sections, each on its petal's colour.

The tiles open the pages the screen's rows open, through the rows
themselves, so launches, titles and metrics stay as they were. The rows
stay in the screen, hidden, for search.

The display face is Google Sans Flex with rounded terminals, cut down to
Latin (OFL 1.1, licenses/GoogleSansFlex-OFL.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
